Third-Party Components

Choreograph vendors no third-party source. Its dependencies are installed
from npm at the versions pinned in pnpm-lock.yaml, each under its own
license; a distribution that bundles node_modules carries their license
files and notices with them. The agent framework Choreograph wraps:

- pi (@earendil-works/pi-agent-core, @earendil-works/pi-ai, from npm)
  MIT License
  Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner
  https://github.com/earendil-works/pi

The local package built by deploy/package-local.sh also bundles, under
prime/, a Sophia fork of Prime Agent, the agent body Choreograph runs. It is
distributed under its own LICENSE, which travels with it:

- Prime Agent (sophia-agent fork)
  MIT License
  Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner
  Copyright (c) 2026 Prime Intellect
  https://github.com/PrimeIntellect-ai/prime-agent
